MewStage vendor patch design-space/0001 (third_party/NOTICE): a window frame drawn to a surface whose scale is below
1 derives its client DIPs from the surface's own scale (pixels / scale), not pixels / max(1, scale). The clamp made
an embedded host at 1280x720 showing a 1920x1080 design-space layout clip and cull a third of it. The whole-frame
area heuristic in Window.Retained uses the same unclamped scale. Applies after allocation/0004 when that category is
present; the hunks also apply to the unpatched file.

--- a/Controls/Window.cs
+++ b/Controls/Window.cs
@@ -3010,9 +3010,13 @@
             throw new ArgumentNullException(nameof(surface));
         }
 
+        // MewStage vendor patch design-space/0001: divide by the surface's own scale. Clamping it to at least 1 made a surface drawn
+        // at a scale below 1 (an embedded host fitting a 1920x1080 layout into 1280x720, scale 2/3) report only
+        // pixels-many DIPs, so the frame's clip and cull viewport covered two thirds of the layout.
+        double surfaceScale = surface.DpiScale > 0 ? surface.DpiScale : 1.0;
         var clientSizeDip = new Size(
-            surface.PixelWidth / Math.Max(1.0, surface.DpiScale),
-            surface.PixelHeight / Math.Max(1.0, surface.DpiScale));
+            surface.PixelWidth / surfaceScale,
+            surface.PixelHeight / surfaceScale);
 
         if (!TryRenderFrameWithOverlay(surface, clientSizeDip))
         {
